# dev-only test assets for the photo funnel (never ship a face in the repo)
public/photoread-test*.webp
supabase/.temp
# Env files. `.env.production` is committed ON PURPOSE — every value in it is
# public by design (Supabase anon key, PostHog project key, Meta pixel id) and
# GitHub Pages builds have nowhere else to read them from. Everything else with
# secrets in it stays out, and the rule that keeps this safe is NOT this file:
#
#   NEVER give a server secret a VITE_ prefix.
#
# Vite inlines every VITE_ variable into the client bundle, so such a secret
# ships to every visitor whether or not the file is committed. Server secrets
# live in Supabase Vault and are read through unloop_get_secret.
# `npm run check:secrets` (blocking in CI) enforces both ends of that rule.
.env
.env.*
!.env.production
*.local
.DS_Store
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
